{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547153-what-have-you-done-with-the-apocryphal-exalted","id":1547153,"title":"What have you done with the Apocryphal Exalted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-19T13:02:55-08:00","id":1547153,"title":"What have you done with the Apocryphal Exalted?","content":"So by Apocryphal I mean Hearteaters, Dream-Souled and Umbral Exalted but if someone had cool ideas for the Revellers of Isidoros and Nightmares of Oramus from Exalted vs. World of Darkness or the Demake, I'd be interested in that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-19T16:11:53-08:00","id":1547157,"title":"","content":"Minor thing, but I did an <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Y1AyBME820JsZMNmer_8_kpSt0ig0wUdHak9EsoDv9s/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">ExWoD conversion</a> for the Dream-Souled a while back. Also comes with Celestial-play options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-19T20:46:50-08:00","id":1547159,"title":"","content":"Actually working on a game with a Hearteater as the major villain. Partially because when I was talking with one of the players they thought the idea was cool. The other being it gave me an interesting mechanic to inject into the operatives and minions of the villain while the group tries to stop the Hearteater's group from taking over the kingdom they're in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-19T21:47:01-08:00","id":1547160,"title":"","content":"While it petered-out, I had a Hearteater as a long term NPC who the PCs would have as a more straight-up antagonist/villain later on, just never got to that point.<br /> <br /> Currently in a Dragon-Blooded campaign on the way to Greyfalls, one of the PCs has regularly been conspiring with an Dream-Souled NPC with plans of eventually undermining House Cynis if possible.<br /> <br /> I have sitting about notes also for some comics/stories/illustrations involving a Hearteater and Umbral Exalt who are total enemies and have an interlinked story and such. Something about the antagonist of the pair being the one with beautiful clear white aurora light while the protagnoist has the shadowmancy and soulsteel reaver daiklave was just kind of an appealing project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-20T10:26:37-08:00","id":1547165,"title":"","content":"So my Exalted Essence game has a former Auroral Exalt imprisoned at the heart of the island by her Twilight Caste husband who was trying to cure her condition and now thousands of years later the containment measures have decayed enough that an extremely powerful Hearteater has some limited awareness of her surroundings and ability to take pawns. Now her husband's returned to her in a new incarnation and it seems her millennia of struggle will end soon... one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T07:52:51-08:00","id":1547199,"title":"","content":"I had some ideas for Auroral Caste Attributes.<br /> <br /> <b>Borealis Caste:</b> Strength, Charisma, Perception<br /> <br /> <b>Australis Caste: </b>Dexterity, Manipulation, Intelligence<br /> <br /> <b>Paraselene Caste: </b>Stamina, Appearance, Wits.<br /> <br /> Paraselene is associated with a phenomenon in the skies related to the moon, but auroras in general are caused by the sun's activities. <br /> <br /> I also play a Hearteater in a MUSH rp named Deryl. He's a Thornish mercenary that fled the city and accompanied a Cathak dragon alongside a few other sellswords. They were betrayed by having their docked ships burnt by the dynast while he and his bodyguards escaped through the last ship, leaving the mercenary band behind and await their fates in the hands of undead.<br /> <br /> Deryl was the last one standing but he escaped and fled to a forest that's a bordermarch. While fearing that zombies and fair folk may get him, he saw an opal skeleton holding a daiklave which he hopes to use but he touched the bones, turning him into a Hearteater<br /> <br /> Suddenly the ghost of his predecessor appeared and congratulated him, taking Deryl under his tutelage. The ghost mentor taught him how to pawn people, but Deryl was a bit disturbed but tempted at the thought of it. His mentor also tried to teach him questionable and self centered philosophies which disgusted him, forcing him to leave his mentor.<br /> <br /> His mentor taunted and warned him that no chosen will trust him and he will forever be scorned and hated by them, since he himself was betrayed by a Lunar who snitched him to Lookshy. He also called him foolish for trying to deny his hunger since he refuses to feed on people's free will. Deryl walked alone and struggled with his hunger until he saw Thornish refugees being extorted by bandits.<br /> <br /> The bandits became his first pawns and he began targetting people he deems as &quot;sinners&quot;. He eventually created a new mercenary company of pawns called the &quot;Devoured Sinners Menagerie&quot; whom he also uses to protect Thornish refugees from Mask's forces and he even gathered some of them to a camp in the Hundred Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> He hopes for his hunger to never drive him to enslave innocence but sometimes he sees himself as just as wicked as the deathknights due to self loathing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T15:22:59-08:00","id":1547225,"title":"","content":"I have sketched a secret demonic cult in Uiluru, that claims among other things the Font of Glories springs in origin of the Three Spheres Cataclysm and the spilled but still vital and roiling ichor of SWLIHN and the rogue Sovereigns leading it are inspired by the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Defiler_Caste\" target=\"_blank\">Defilers</a> from back in 2e. Is that apocryphal enough? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Have also toyed a bit with the idea of settings from Shards of the Exalted Dream as &quot;alternities&quot; acessible through the fractal mirror maze of Szoreny, making contact/crossover with those &quot;worlds&quot; and the peculiar exalted that inhabit them, possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> But speaking of the three aforementioned Exalt types, i have experimented much with the Dream Souled, in particular with the Bugiber, the peculiar fruit of the many experimentations in lineage-building of an exiled Lintha prince turned Dream Souled, in the time between Contagion and Fae invasion, taking the form of an unique extended band of reavers and traders of sea, sky, wyld, underworld and beyond that stand in a space not unlike Sovereigns or a Dragon-Blooded household.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T05:48:38-08:00","id":1547259,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of having a dream souled NPC messing with the PCs during the night with the social influence system. My NPC would need Face Changing Glamour to disguise their identity as they interact with the PC in the real world, Midnight Guest Invitation so they can show up in the PC's dream to attempt their influence, and whispering to the sleeper to allow entrance to the PC's dreams from miles away.<br /> <br /> They would also need enough social influence tools to not get stomped by the PC. But having a possibly antagonistic NPC show up in the character's dreams and contest them with roleplaying and the influence system, that's golden. You asked what we have done rather than what we want to do but be assured next time I run a game; this will be in the has done column before the end of session 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 12-26-2024, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T09:17:45-08:00","id":1547333,"title":"","content":"Not as such, I'm using the Dream-Souled mechanics as the basis of a Lloroch character a pre-human race that was a lion spirit living under Feverfew Valley on the Blessed Isle in previous editions.<br /> <br /> My take on it is a being that has a vast racial memory that stretches back to a time before humans existed, powerful telepathy and some ability to control the weather but is still in essence a cat. She sleeps most of the time (not necessarily a state that's a disadvantage to her) and can be bribed with food and toys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T06:29:35-07:00","id":1549499,"title":"","content":"As of Pillars of Creation we've now got our first solid picture of what the Spoken were like, it's intended for Essence but there's familiar concepts that could enable their use in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}